{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1180798-kickstarter-preview-discussion-core-01-04","id":1180798,"title":"Kickstarter Preview Discussion: Core 01-04","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-30T10:33:05-08:00","id":1180798,"title":"Kickstarter Preview Discussion: Core 01-04","content":"The first backer-only Update contains a link to the first section of the Trinity Continuum core rulebook, including the Introduction, some artifacts of the setting, and character creation. Feel free to discuss below.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T12:17:20-08:00","id":1180840,"title":"","content":"Cool so far! I never read the original Trinity books, but I think the concept of Talents and flux manipulation and stuff is a very funny and great way to make those kinds of larger than life characters possible.<br /> <br /> I like the skill list!<br /> <br /> I\u2019m a little unsure about Edges, which seem to be the Merits of the game? Overall I think they have fun text, but there\u2019s a few there which feel like they don\u2019t have enough meat to them and they just feel like enhancement grabs.<br /> <br /> I noticed that there\u2019s a two dot Edge that gives people stacking +1 Soft Armor, which if I remember right is worth like 3 dice on a dice pool? Maybe the dice pools slew higher than Scion, but I am a little worried that something like that feels like a must-have for any character. I think maybe attaching a prerequisite like Stamina 3 or something like some other Edges have could help.<br /> <br /> Just musing outloud, could be a little houserile for anyone else concerned about that!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Violet Green, Freelancer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","name":"VioletDreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T12:19:03-08:00","id":1180842,"title":"","content":"Do we anticipate bringing in characters, powers, or other elements from other Onyx Path games?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T13:22:47-08:00","id":1180865,"title":"","content":"For now, I'm just going to watch this thread. <br /> <br /> For the most part I am very unfamiliar with Trinity. I've got the basics of the setting through the TV Tropes pages and the &quot;I know so little&quot; topic on this forum. So I think I get the basics. <br /> <br /> So while I watch this thread, can someone sell me on Trinity? What do you like about it? I may or may not pledge so I kinda want a feel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T14:16:16-08:00","id":1180882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1180798-kickstarter-preview-discussion-core-01-04?p=1180842#post1180842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we anticipate bringing in characters, powers, or other elements from other Onyx Path games?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Trinity Continuum settings are already looking pretty huge and open ended. They're more likely to do their own take on &quot;ancient gods &amp; heroes&quot; via Novas in the Aegis setting than have some sort of Scion crossover.<br /> <br /> And obviously the stuff Onyx Path doesn't own itself aren't going to crossover, so that's all the World of Darkness, Chronicles of Darkness, and Exalted stuff off the table - as all that is licensed from White Wolf. And Pugmire and Cavaliers are creator owned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T17:56:46-08:00","id":1180948,"title":"","content":"Lookimg forward to more info on stunts. Seems very heavy if u have to look at a table everytime u succed on a roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T18:35:34-08:00","id":1180962,"title":"","content":"Will Adventure and Abberant be their own kickstarters?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T18:56:40-08:00","id":1180968,"title":"","content":"I cnr help but think its like a lighter world of darkness. Which honestly makes sense but it still brings a smile to my face. <br /> <br /> I like the first chapter. Nice set up on what the theme is. <br /> <br /> I did notice though that Quantum isn't mentioned in glossary. <br /> <br /> The setting chapter is interesting. It very much gives me a aberrant vibe, which had me grinning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T12:12:33-08:00","id":1181186,"title":"","content":"This is kind of a strange question, but I noticed it both here in the scion preview and I'm curious. Why exactly is action-adventure/combat it's own chapter separate from the general system chapter? So far as I'm aware just about every white wolf/onyx path publication has always had all the rules in one chapter, I get that combat generally has more word count devoted to it, but it still seems like you could collapse them into one chapter. Is there a particular reason for the divide?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T01:12:24-08:00","id":1181347,"title":"","content":"I'm impressed with what we've got so far. There's a few bits I disagree with, but none of it's a big deal. Compared to Scion, the whole thing feels a bit more complete too - Scion is littered with bits of Trinity Continuum (Skill names, etc.), which makes me think that while the writing is finished, they're still at the point of compiling their document together. If the rest of the Trinity books are at this stage, I'd consider it ready to go for a game, whereas I've still got a lot of questions about Scion.<br /> <br /> Either way, in the next month or two, it looks like I'm going to be running something Storypath.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lionmanguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1180798-kickstarter-preview-discussion-core-01-04?p=1181186#post1181186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is kind of a strange question, but I noticed it both here in the scion preview and I'm curious. Why exactly is action-adventure/combat it's own chapter separate from the general system chapter? So far as I'm aware just about every white wolf/onyx path publication has always had all the rules in one chapter, I get that combat generally has more word count devoted to it, but it still seems like you could collapse them into one chapter. Is there a particular reason for the divide?</div> </div> </div> </div>My guess is that it's a deliberate tone choice - World of Darkness is a horror game that often has combat. Storypath is designed for action-adventure, and physical conflict is front and centre.<br /> <br /> Essentially, it's leaning into the argument that the rules a game emphasises should reflect it's intended playstyle.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Questions though: How many Short-term Aspirations does the group need to achieve for the group xp? It feels like it was written assuming they only had 1 short term, but since they have two you get ambiguity: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All players achieve their short-term aspirations in the same Session </div> </div> </div>There's a plural there. Does that mean all players need to achieve <i>both</i> of their short-term aspirations?<br /> <br /> My reading is that it triggers when &quot;All players achieve <i>at least one of</i> their short-term aspirations in the same Session&quot;, but I'd like to be sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2649,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","user":"Tarion","date":". 02-01-2018, 06:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T13:22:09-08:00","id":1181479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1180798-kickstarter-preview-discussion-core-01-04?p=1181347#post1181347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> EDIT: Questions though: How many Short-term Aspirations does the group need to achieve for the group xp? It feels like it was written assuming they only had 1 short term, but since they have two you get ambiguity:<br /> <br /> There's a plural there. Does that mean all players need to achieve <i>both</i> of their short-term aspirations?<br /> <br /> My reading is that it triggers when &quot;All players achieve <i>at least one of</i> their short-term aspirations in the same Session&quot;, but I'd like to be sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's correct, and I'll likely go through and see if that needs a clarification. The assumption is that everyone is likely to get one of their short term aspirations completed each session, though maybe not quite both of them. It's there to reward people for helping their group achieve their goals.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Danielle Lauzon, Requiem Developer, Storypath Guru, freelance writer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6155-impernious","name":"impernious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T08:33:42-08:00","id":1181668,"title":"","content":"The second backer-only Update (Update #5) contains a link to the second section of the Trinity Continuum core rulebook, including the Chapter 3: Storypath System, and part of Chapter Four: Combat and Equipment. Feel free to discuss below.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T17:15:53-08:00","id":1181860,"title":"","content":"I'll repost some of my thoughts from the KS comments. <br /> <br /> Regarding Initiative: <br /> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">This system seems to use a sort of hybrid between traditional Storyteller initiative and popcorn initiative as used in Cortex Heroic. <br /> So, everyone rolls for initiative in a pretty normal manner, ranking the most successes rolled as the best initiative score. Where it differs from previous OPP/WW initiative systems is that player characters and SG characters don't go based on their initiative score. When a player slot comes up, the players determine which of them will go in that slot. Unlike popcorn initiative systems, a person who has gone, does not determine who goes next.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Example: Everyone rolls the lower of Athletics + Cunning or Empathy + Dexterity, and the rolls shake out like this.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Tick ratings <br /> Player Character 1: 6 successes <br /> Storyguide Character 1: 5 successes <br /> SC 2: 4 successes <br /> PC 2: 2 successes</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">That gets turned into slots <br /> PC slot <br /> SC slot <br /> SC slot <br /> PC slot</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">When a PC slot comes up, the group decides as a matter of group strategy who among them should act. When a SC slot comes up, the Storyguide determine which Storyguide character should act.<br /> It's a bit like FFG's Star Wars initiative system. <br /> <br /> Regarding actions: <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I've been thinking about the mixed actions, and I really think it's clever how it's not &quot;multiple actions&quot; like Storyteller, nor does it absolutely prevent simultaneous actions as in Storytelling. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">It'll be interesting to see what rules and powers hook into Mixed Actions. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I also noticed that reflexive actions seem to be different in Storypath vs Storytelling. In Storytelling, I think you can do a reflexive action at any time. In Storypath, reflexive actions can only be taken when the player has the Focus.<br /> <br /> Going to have to finish reading combat next. Haven't yet grokked enhancement or stunts. </span></span></span><br /> </span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T17:50:42-08:00","id":1181868,"title":"","content":"The rules feel really clean, polished and well-presented here! I love it. Amazing job, corebook team!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Violet Green, Freelancer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","name":"VioletDreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T19:53:42-08:00","id":1181897,"title":"","content":"Are normal none super science items considered to be Rank 1 for purposes of making them with the crafting system?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T05:45:03-08:00","id":1181973,"title":"","content":"Does the Preview give the (more or less) final version of character creation? I ask because of the major differences between how Paths work in Scion vs. how they\u2019re described in the Preview. Scion, for example, ranks each of the three paths according to importance and gives points to Path Skills in accordance to the ranking. In contrast, the approach in Continuum is...kind of hard to follow, so at the very least it needs a polish.<br /> <br /> Of course I realize that there\u2019ll be differences between the two games, but I was surprised that they differed so much in such core essentials. \u2014Jim","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4310-jagardner","name":"jagardner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T12:18:53-08:00","id":1182039,"title":"","content":"I think you're overcomplicating TC by comparing it to Scion. TC is, if anything, much simpler. You don't worry about ranking your Paths, you just put 3 skill dots in any of the related Skills (In any combination you'd like. Could be 3 into one skill, 1 into 3 different skills etc. Doesn't matter, so long as it's 3 total) <br /> <br /> It's lighter on the skill points than Scion, but that's (Presumably) because there's more stuff to come with the Template, later in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T13:34:13-08:00","id":1182054,"title":"","content":"I'd be interested in understanding the rational behind disallowing skill tricks on starting characters. Reaching a 3rd dot in a skill is the only way listed for one to get a skill trick in a skill, but if you start with 3 dots in a skill can the character never receive the trick for that dot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T13:40:17-08:00","id":1182057,"title":"","content":"I more or less got that,but still: you pick four skills with each Path, except they can\u2019t all get dots, and maybe only one of them gets dots, except you can add dots later if you feel like, except that you could add your later dots to brand new skills that aren\u2019t associated with Paths. So you might well have dotless skills that are kind of yours even though they aren\u2019t developed, and they sort of kind of get boosted if you add dots to the Path they\u2019re associated with, rather than to the skills themselves. But this means you have to remember which skills are associated with which Paths.. Some dotless skills will *really* be dotless, and some won\u2019t quite be because they get a boost from being associated with a high-power Path.<br /> <br /> Or maybe I\u2019m wrong. As I say, I think the write-up needs work to spell things out more clearly. \u2014Jim","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4310-jagardner","name":"jagardner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T13:43:31-08:00","id":1182058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1180798-kickstarter-preview-discussion-core-01-04?p=1182039#post1182039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're overcomplicating TC by comparing it to Scion. TC is, if anything, much simpler. You don't worry about ranking your Paths, you just put 3 skill dots in any of the related Skills (In any combination you'd like. Could be 3 into one skill, 1 into 3 different skills etc. Doesn't matter, so long as it's 3 total)<br /> <br /> It's lighter on the skill points than Scion, but that's (Presumably) because there's more stuff to come with the Template, later in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically, Trinity Paths have ratings that maybe improved, while Scion paths may not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T10:33:18-08:00","id":1182977,"title":"","content":"The third backer-only Update (Update #8) contains a link to the third section of the Trinity Continuum core rulebook, including the rest of Chapter Four: Combat and Equipment, and Chapter Five: The Storyguide. Feel free to discuss below.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T14:45:41-08:00","id":1183046,"title":"","content":"I love the vehicle/spaceship rules!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T16:35:03-08:00","id":1183088,"title":"","content":"Like the personnal weapon Idea. Although have not all of the rules","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T12:52:16-08:00","id":1183668,"title":"","content":"So far I like what I am seeing,but I'll need to play with it a bit to get a feel for how it will work in an actual game. Organizationally, I think it might be helpful to have the section on regular weapons and vehicles before the section on upgrades and inventions. And, on that note a few questions:<br /> <br /> 1. To what extent will Aeon have pre-stated items. I can see that the system contemplates individualized items for all characters, but there were some cool &quot;standard&quot; items in 1e.<br /> <br /> 2. I find the Quality tag a bit confusing. The 2 point version adds 1 extra tags slot, and the 3 point version adds 2 extra slots, but for that to mean anything the intial 2 or 3 slot expendature for the Quality tag must not count. So, am I correct to assume that a character with two wealth could buy an item with the 2 point Quality tag, and then apply 3 points of tags to the item?<br /> <br /> 3. Concerning how the invention system interacts with the regular equipment. Should we be designing a regular item, and then adding the enhancements and flaws from the invention system to produce the final form of a piece of equipment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T10:35:35-08:00","id":1184002,"title":"","content":"The fourth backer-only Update (Update #11) contains a link to the fourth and final section of the Trinity Continuum core rulebook, including Chapter Six: Talents, and Chapter Seven: Gifts. Feel free to discuss below.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T11:49:59-08:00","id":1184028,"title":"","content":"So just to be clear on terminology, a Talent is a subset of Inspired, replacing the old term Daredevil, and Stalwarts and Mesmerists are still going to be around when Adventure! comes out right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T11:59:01-08:00","id":1184031,"title":"","content":"It's either that, or \u201cmesmerist\u201d is just another name for \u201cpsiad\u201d and \u201cstalwart\u201d is just another name for \u201cstealth nova\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T12:22:42-08:00","id":1184039,"title":"","content":"I'm somewhat lost as to when something should be a Skill Trick, when it should be an Edge, and when it should be a Gift. For instance, the Hidden Arsenal Skill Trick lets you activate it in order to have a backup weapon even after you've seemingly been disarmed. Why is this not a Gift? It certainly sounds like the sort of thing one could do with Dramatic Editing, and I've always pictured Gifts as specialized applications of Dramatic Editing. Conversely, An Extension of Myself (the first sample Gift under Aim) strikes me as something that would work better as an Edge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T13:35:13-08:00","id":1184059,"title":"","content":"Is Source (like mentioned in Behold the Halo) the power type/fuel used by people (so Inspiration, Psi, or Quantum)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T14:25:40-08:00","id":1184080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lionmanguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1180798-kickstarter-preview-discussion-core-01-04?p=1184028#post1184028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So just to be clear on terminology, a Talent is a subset of Inspired, replacing the old term Daredevil, and Stalwarts and Mesmerists are still going to be around when Adventure! comes out right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t know about the terminology that will be used but it was confirmed a while ago that the Trinity Core would introduce rules for Paramorphs, Aeon the rules for Psychomorphs, Aberrant the rules for Eximorphs, and Adventure! would have rules for lower powered versions of all three.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T15:05:01-08:00","id":1184096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1180798-kickstarter-preview-discussion-core-01-04?p=1184031#post1184031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's either that, or \u201cmesmerist\u201d is just another name for \u201cpsiad\u201d and \u201cstalwart\u201d is just another name for \u201cstealth nova\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a side note on stealth Novas, while i\u2019m sure they will still be a thing - I expect they will get comparatively less attention in the Aberrant era this time specifically because Talents are a thing. The Directive for example I imagine is going to be geared toward a Talent centered play Allegiance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T15:23:42-08:00","id":1184108,"title":"","content":"They barely got any attention in the Aberrant era the first time around.<br /> <br /> For the record, I'm using \u201cstealth Nova\u201d as shorthand for \u201csomeone who uses the rules for Novas, but restricted to just Scaled attributes and associated Enhancements \u2014 no Quantum Powers\u201d. And to me, that feels like a remarkably close approximation to Adventure!'s stalwarts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T15:37:40-08:00","id":1184114,"title":"","content":"\u2018Stealth novas\u2019 didn\u2019t tend to exist in 1e Aberrant era because of the presence of all the Novas. The presence of Quantum forces tended to cause others with the potential to become novas to erupt and become novas themselves. This wasn\u2019t the case for psions in the AEon era - possibly because humanity just hadn\u2019t evolved far enough to unlock full power yet (hence the Prometheus chambers), and possibly because psi just doesn\u2019t have the same effect as quantum.<br /> <br /> It was possible to play a nova character who just had skills, attributes and enhancements, but it didn\u2019t tend to be a common choice.<br /> <br /> 2e Aberrant hasn\u2019t happened yet, so who knows if this will still be the case, but if things do work as similarly to how they did in 1e, \u2018stealth novas\u2019 are more likely to exist in other eras, when full power novas aren\u2019t around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T16:59:28-08:00","id":1184136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1180798-kickstarter-preview-discussion-core-01-04?p=1184039#post1184039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm somewhat lost as to when something should be a Skill Trick, when it should be an Edge, and when it should be a Gift</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still digesting things, but this seems... kinda inevitable? If Talents are supposed to be hard to tell apart from extremely competent/lucky people that can't directly tap into Flux, then their powers are going to be hard to slot neatly into a line on what should be what.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T06:18:37-08:00","id":1184356,"title":"","content":"I'm running through some sample chargen and I've hit a snag. Quick question about this line in Manuscript 4, page 9, second to last pararaph:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Talents start with three Gifts (p. XX), each of which comes from her three Paths.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> I'm seeing Gifts listed under each Allegiance / Society Path, but not mentioned at all under each Origin and Role Paths. As I missing something? Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T06:33:20-08:00","id":1184363,"title":"","content":"Yeah. There's a section listing an Attribute and a set of Skills for each Origin and Role Path: when choosing Gifts, the ones tied to those traits count as being associated with that Path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T07:10:13-08:00","id":1184376,"title":"","content":"Cheers Dataweaver, I'll go back and re-read that section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T18:17:19-08:00","id":1184578,"title":"","content":"What are the primary differences between Division 9 and the National Office of Emergency Research?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T08:14:48-08:00","id":1184739,"title":"","content":"Question: If you have the Superior Trait Edge, can your bonus attribute from your Moment of Inspiration push you up to 6?<br /> If (as I assume) the answer is no, probably that should be called out and like with the Favored Approach att bonuses.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T08:19:12-08:00","id":1184741,"title":"","content":"Also, What should your total number of Attribute Points be at character creation?<br /> I'm getting 25 for a baseline, 26 for a talent. Is this right?<br /> <br /> I could really use a streamlined character creation summery (I assume the final book will have one, just not in the preview docs).<br /> <br /> 1 dot in each att to start - 9<br /> 6/4/2 distributed - 12 (21 total)<br /> +1 to each Focused Approach - 3 (24 t)<br /> +1 to any one att finishing touches - 1 (25 t)<br /> <br /> Talent +1 based on Moment of Inspiration - 1 (26 total)<br /> <br /> Seem right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T10:35:00-08:00","id":1184790,"title":"","content":"How should we handle scale differences between characters and their gear? Guns are listed as scale 2, while psions are scale 3. When a psion shoots something with a regular gun is that attack considered scale 2 or scale 3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T10:31:13-08:00","id":1185251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lionmanguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1180798-kickstarter-preview-discussion-core-01-04?p=1184578#post1184578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the primary differences between Division 9 and the National Office of Emergency Research?</div> </div> </div> </div>9 is focused on high-tech crime and terrorism, the NOER on Flux and paraphysical phenomena. There's some overlap as technology gets more advanced and people use Flux abilities aggressively, but also areas that only one or the other would investigate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T16:31:24-08:00","id":1185392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lionmanguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1180798-kickstarter-preview-discussion-core-01-04?p=1184578#post1184578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the primary differences between Division 9 and the National Office of Emergency Research?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To put it in TV terms, think of 9 as early &quot;Agents of SHIELD&quot; and NOER as &quot;Fringe.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T09:04:41-08:00","id":1185602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythicFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1180798-kickstarter-preview-discussion-core-01-04?p=1185392#post1185392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To put it in TV terms, think of 9 as early &quot;Agents of SHIELD&quot; and NOER as &quot;Fringe.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd put some of <b>Fringe</b> in the overlap due to the group using fringe science as a weapon, though the visitors from parallel universes are more of an NOER problem. (The Asgardian superweapon and universe-jumping &quot;ghost&quot; in <b>Agents Of S.H.I.E.L.D.</b> season one would be too.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T09:57:30-08:00","id":1185625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Craig Oxbrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1180798-kickstarter-preview-discussion-core-01-04?p=1185602#post1185602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd put some of <b>Fringe</b> in the overlap due to the group using fringe science as a weapon, though the visitors from parallel universes are more of an NOER problem. (The Asgardian superweapon and universe-jumping &amp;quot;ghost&amp;quot; in <b>Agents Of S.H.I.E.L.D.</b> season one would be too.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair, I was kind of generalizing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T11:28:20-08:00","id":1185670,"title":"","content":"Can you name the Allegiances that were not included in the Core? Ian mentioned (it's somewhere in this forum) that he had 17 Allegiances; the Core only describes 13.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T16:57:58-08:00","id":1185776,"title":"","content":"No, sorry.<br /> <br /> Discussing cut material never really ends well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T04:00:17-08:00","id":1185877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1180798-kickstarter-preview-discussion-core-01-04?p=1185776#post1185776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, sorry.<br /> <br /> Discussing cut material never really ends well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fair enough. Will we see them in future supplements or are they cut for good?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T14:37:49-08:00","id":1186075,"title":"","content":"We'll see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T14:44:57-08:00","id":1186080,"title":"","content":"Aka posted by me on the kickstarter but it's important to me. <br /> <br /> May I ask from someone who completely gets it to explain a but more how damage corresponds to health loss, the whole health system, and it's healing. This is one of those areas that hasn't clicked for me yet. (I much prefer a hit point system to be honest.) But I love the system so far and so I want it to click!<br /> <br /> It's a problem I have had in all storyteller incarnations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T17:02:25-08:00","id":1188022,"title":"","content":"I have a question: in the Trinity Core Preview 1 page 29 the cost for Path is 15 Experience, but in the page 32, under &quot;Advancement with Paths&quot; the cost is 5 Experience. What is the correct cost?<br /> <br /> Thanks for help me!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/437-shadowninja","name":"shadowninja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T11:00:25-08:00","id":1189934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shadowninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1180798-kickstarter-preview-discussion-core-01-04?p=1188022#post1188022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question: in the Trinity Core Preview 1 page 29 the cost for Path is 15 Experience, but in the page 32, under &quot;Advancement with Paths&quot; the cost is 5 Experience. What is the correct cost?<br /> <br /> Thanks for help me!</div> </div> </div> </div>It's supposed to be 15 points. That is one of those things that we were fiddling with right before the text went to Kickstarter, so we'll make sure we clean up any stray references.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Danielle Lauzon, Requiem Developer, Storypath Guru, freelance writer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6155-impernious","name":"impernious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T01:00:47-08:00","id":1190169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Craig Oxbrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1180798-kickstarter-preview-discussion-core-01-04?p=1185251#post1185251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 9 is focused on high-tech crime and terrorism, the NOER on Flux and paraphysical phenomena. There's some overlap as technology gets more advanced and people use Flux abilities aggressively, but also areas that only one or the other would investigate.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> At this point there's also the clear distinction that NOER is US government, and 9 is a private-intelligence-contractor that works with many different national and multinational entities. So the fact that they overlap in purview works as they're positioned to be competitors in those cases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T11:28:29-08:00","id":1192323,"title":"","content":"I was looking at the Path Creation section of the combined Core that starts on page 30 and the discussion of Contacts and using Connections has some inconsistencies. For example, the Contacts section says you can allocate (Path) dots between multiple Contacts, but the using Connections section says that all Connections have a rating equal to (Path). <br /> <br /> Also, if your Contacts get an additional Tag for each dot you give to them and give Enhancement equal to their dots, then buying one Contact who does everything is strictly better than splitting them up into multiple single dot Contacts. There doesn\u2019t seem to be any mechanical down side to knowing a Fixer who knows everyone and can get you anything, instead of knowing five people who can each help you out in a different area.<br /> <br /> That section could use some review.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T19:32:53-08:00","id":1192925,"title":"","content":"I'm putting this here as I didn't want to simply create a new thread for this and we'll this is a Kickstarter thread. <br /> <br /> But I totally enjoyed the \u00c6on Developer Notes posted by John Snead on the kickstarter (and any similar comments made by others). <br /> <br /> When Trinity Continuum Aberrant comes around having such a similar thing would be quite beneficial to seeing where things are going. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Ps. As a note I have reread the two files, it's just so brilliant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T15:40:40-08:00","id":1193334,"title":"","content":"Would anybody be willing to present some examples of items built for the modern setting using the Super-Science rules? I'm having a hard time fully parsing how they should work and it feels like examples might be helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Violet Green, Freelancer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","name":"VioletDreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T10:39:17-07:00","id":1198744,"title":"","content":"I can't help but think, especially after hearing the sad news today of the Galatea explosion, may those on it rest in peace, that it would be cool if said space station had a segment in the news portion of the core book. Nothing major just a nifty mention. Hehe","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T19:45:31-07:00","id":1198944,"title":"","content":"Isn't it a bit much to have Skill Tricks, Edges (enhanced), and Gifts? Seem kind of cluttered and confusing what something should be if you homebrew.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T21:31:12-07:00","id":1198959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1180798-kickstarter-preview-discussion-core-01-04?p=1198944#post1198944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't it a bit much to have Skill Tricks, Edges (enhanced), and Gifts? Seem kind of cluttered and confusing what something should be if you homebrew.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not really. Things that should only be available to Talents go into Gifts. For the other two it's just a question of whether it builds directly on an Skill or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T22:37:47-07:00","id":1198966,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind also that Skill Tricks aren\u2019t available at character creation. They come later to specifically reflect character advancement and in-game mastery of their field.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T08:04:03-07:00","id":1205595,"title":"","content":"I didn't have access to Trinity previews, but regarding skills, i was looking the Character sheets on this thread (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1189011-psion-character-sheet\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...haracter-sheet</a>), and was wondering: Since all kind of skills were merged on single ones, like Science, humanities, culture and larceny, shouldn't Persuasion and Command be merged on a single one like &quot;Influence&quot; or something like that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9243,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9243-oparra","user":"oparra","date":". 04-11-2018, 11:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9243-oparra","name":"oparra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T00:04:09-07:00","id":1206308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>oparra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1180798-kickstarter-preview-discussion-core-01-04?p=1205595#post1205595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since all kind of skills were merged on single ones, like Science, humanities, culture and larceny, shouldn't Persuasion and Command be merged on a single one like &quot;Influence&quot; or something like that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Persuasion and Command cover different ways of influencing a person. Persuasion is used to manipulate, whereas Command is intended to give orders (often, but not necessarily, from a position of authority) and expect them to the followed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T07:32:38-07:00","id":1206432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythicFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1180798-kickstarter-preview-discussion-core-01-04?p=1206308#post1206308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Persuasion and Command cover different ways of influencing a person. Persuasion is used to manipulate, whereas Command is intended to give orders (often, but not necessarily, from a position of authority) and expect them to the followed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I know. And I agree. But, i think that this kind of difference from manipulate, lead and even intimidate, still converge into a single skill that deal with &quot;your ability to influence people&quot;, the same way that culture have different fields of activities to &quot;know, understand and produce arts&quot;, or Larceny to &quot;Trick, mislead or deceive people&quot;. IMHO, since skills have more &quot;wide&quot; fields, i believe that both persuade and command could be merged...<br /> <br /> Sorry for any mistakes. My english is not very good...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9243,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9243-oparra","user":"oparra","date":". 04-13-2018, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9243-oparra","name":"oparra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T07:34:33-07:00","id":1216112,"title":"","content":"In both the Core and Aeon books, I don't think i found any rules covering starting gear?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24178-heartless-koschei","name":"Heartless Koschei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T08:52:35-07:00","id":1216157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heartless Koschei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1180798-kickstarter-preview-discussion-core-01-04?p=1216112#post1216112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In both the Core and Aeon books, I don't think i found any rules covering starting gear?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless it\u2019s some kind of super-device, general possessions would be whatever is justified by your Paths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T17:04:40-07:00","id":1245240,"title":"","content":"Mixed actions in combat, page 110 states (in short)<br /> 3 actions<br /> Escape from chair (dif 1)<br /> Disarm thug (dif 1)<br /> kick bomb out window (dif 0)<br /> Example says this requires 5 successes.<br /> <br /> Difficulty, page 74 states:<br /> Every action has a level of Difficulty. For many actions that level is 1. The level of Difficulty is the number of successes a player must spend to overcome how hard the task is. So, for a task with 1 Difficulty, a player needs to roll at least 1 success to complete the task.<br /> <br /> Storypath System preview, page 3 shows a difficulty 3 roll requires a total of three successes to achieve.<br /> <br /> Do mixed actions require an additional success per action, or is the 5 success requirement listed in error?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24507-baladain","name":"Baladain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T17:45:40-07:00","id":1245245,"title":"","content":"You need to buy off the Difficulty and still have a success per action to make it happen. In the example above, to escape the chair you need to buy off diff 1 and have one success to then escape for a total of 2 successes, to disarm the thug you need to buy off diff 1 and have one success to grab the weapon for a total of 2 successes, then to kick the bomb out the window you need one success as there\u2019s no extra Difficulty to buy off. Total = 5 successes.<br /> <br /> I believe the section on Difficulty on p74 has been clarified that you need to able to spend a success on an action, after difficulty is accounted for, to be able to perform the action. Otherwise, various actions with no additional difficulty would succeed without rolling any successes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T18:48:45-07:00","id":1245272,"title":"","content":"So the system preview diagram should be updated to have 4 as the green number for a difficulty 3 roll?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24507-baladain","name":"Baladain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T15:20:30-07:00","id":1245656,"title":"","content":"Getting to pg 119 and Other forms of Damage, Damage Rating.<br /> The example states &quot;For example, if a character drank a cocktail someone had laced with cyanide (damage rating 5), she would need to make a Stamina + Resolve roll. If she rolled 4 successes, she succeeded, because she exceeded the Difficulty and thus her 3 remaining successes would subtract from the Damage Rating, reducing it from 5 to 2.&quot;<br /> <br /> This seems to contradict the idea that you need to spend a success to buy off the difficulty and have a success per action to make it happen.<br /> <br /> Is this a contradiction, or is the difference that resisting damage is not counted as an action?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24507-baladain","name":"Baladain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}